{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:BringsSurface.OrbitalFourierDecomposition","@type":"LeanModule","name":"BringsSurface.OrbitalFourierDecomposition","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.QIntegerCanonical"],"declarations":22,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:orbital_fourier_decomposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"orbital_fourier_decomposition","kind":"theorem","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/orbital-fourier-decomposition.lean#L189-L201","doc":"**Orbital-dimension count (conditional on `BorromeanQuark`).**\nGiven the Borromean-quark Fourier/SO(3) decomposition of the\nnormal-bundle orbital space, the orbital-space dimension at shell `n`\nis exactly `n²`, and the spin-doubled shell capacity is `2n²`.\n\nDerived from `decomposition_law` (the class field) and the\nunconditional `orbital_dim_eq_square` — a real equation, not `True`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:BorromeanQuark.decomposition_law","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"BorromeanQuark.decomposition_law","kind":"theorem","line":186,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/orbital-fourier-decomposition.lean#L186-L186","doc":"Fourier/SO(3) decomposition law: `dim O_n = Σ_{ℓ<n} dim V_ℓ`, the\nsum of the `SO(3)`-irreducible dimensions `modeSpaceDim ℓ = 2ℓ+1`\nover the admissible modes `ℓ < n` (mode cut-off of §4). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:BorromeanQuark.orbitalDim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"BorromeanQuark.orbitalDim","kind":"def","line":182,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/orbital-fourier-decomposition.lean#L182-L182","doc":"The orbital-space dimension at shell `n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:BorromeanQuark.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"BorromeanQuark.mk","kind":"ctor","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/orbital-fourier-decomposition.lean#L180-L180","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:BorromeanQuark","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"BorromeanQuark","kind":"class","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/orbital-fourier-decomposition.lean#L167-L187","doc":"**Borromean-quark orbital-decomposition class** (conditional input for\n`conj:orbital-fourier-decomposition`).  The conjectural content is the\nFourier/SO(3) realisation of the normal-bundle orbital space: at each\nshell `n` the space `O_n` of admissible normal-bundle sections is the\ndirect sum of the `SO(3)` irreducibles `V_ℓ` over the admissible modes\n`ℓ < n`, so its dimension is the sum of the mode dimensions\n`dim V_ℓ = modeSpaceDim ℓ = 2ℓ+1`.  This `dim`-functional and its\ndecomposition law are the single open input; everything downstream is\nderived.\n\n`sorry`/no-instance is understood as **conjecture**, not missing proof\n(AGENTS.md §3b). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:mode_cutoff_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"mode_cutoff_iff","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/orbital-fourier-decomposition.lean#L128-L131","doc":"Mode cutoff iff: ℓ(ℓ+1) ≤ n(n-1) ↔ ℓ ≤ n-1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:mode_cutoff_conv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"mode_cutoff_conv","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/orbital-fourier-decomposition.lean#L121-L126","doc":"Converse: ℓ ≤ n-1 ⟹ ℓ(ℓ+1) ≤ n(n-1). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:mode_cutoff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"mode_cutoff","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/orbital-fourier-decomposition.lean#L105-L119","doc":"Mode cutoff: ℓ(ℓ+1) ≤ n(n-1) ⟹ ℓ ≤ n-1.\nProof: contrapositive — if ℓ ≥ n then ℓ(ℓ+1) ≥ n(n+1) > n(n-1). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:quantum_count","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"quantum_count","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/orbital-fourier-decomposition.lean#L95-L99","doc":"Count of all quantum numbers (ℓ, m, s) at fixed n:\n2 · n² (two spin states per orbital). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:orbital_count","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"orbital_count","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/orbital-fourier-decomposition.lean#L86-L93","doc":"Count of orbital quantum numbers (ℓ, m) at fixed n:\nΣ_{ℓ=0}^{n-1} (2ℓ+1) = n². ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:magnetic_count","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"magnetic_count","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/orbital-fourier-decomposition.lean#L79-L84","doc":"Count of magnetic quantum numbers at fixed ℓ:\nm ranges from -ℓ to +ℓ, giving 2ℓ+1 values. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QN.hm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QN.hm","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/orbital-fourier-decomposition.lean#L77-L77","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QN.hℓ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QN.hℓ","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/orbital-fourier-decomposition.lean#L76-L76","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QN.s","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QN.s","kind":"def","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/orbital-fourier-decomposition.lean#L75-L75","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QN.m","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QN.m","kind":"def","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/orbital-fourier-decomposition.lean#L74-L74","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QN.ℓ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QN.ℓ","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/orbital-fourier-decomposition.lean#L73-L73","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QN.n","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QN.n","kind":"def","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/orbital-fourier-decomposition.lean#L72-L72","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QN.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QN.mk","kind":"ctor","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/orbital-fourier-decomposition.lean#L71-L71","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QN","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QN","kind":"structure","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/orbital-fourier-decomposition.lean#L70-L77","doc":"A valid set of quantum numbers (n, ℓ, m, s). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:total_states_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"total_states_eq","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/orbital-fourier-decomposition.lean#L61-L64","doc":"Total states per shell including spin: 2n². ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:orbital_dim_eq_square","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"orbital_dim_eq_square","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/orbital-fourier-decomposition.lean#L52-L59","doc":"The orbital space dimension at shell n: Σ_{ℓ=0}^{n-1} (2ℓ+1) = n². ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:modeSpaceDim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"modeSpaceDim","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/orbital-fourier-decomposition.lean#L49-L50","doc":"Dimension of the SO(3) irreducible V_ℓ. ","signatureChunk":0}]}